What does the following snippet print regarding explicit no-arg constructors versus implicit super calls?

```java
class BaseTracker {
    int count = 1;
    BaseTracker() {
        this.count = 5;
    }
}
class SubTracker extends BaseTracker {
    SubTracker() {
        // explicit no-arg constructor without explicit super
    }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SubTracker t = new SubTracker();
        System.out.println(t.count);
    }
}
```

